Project Title
LifeGuard AI: Unified Autonomous Health & Emergency Guardian

Project Overview
LifeGuard AI is an advanced, privacy-first web application designed to act as a 24/7 digital health companion. It seamlessly integrates physical health monitoring, psychological well-being tools, and an SOS emergency response network into a single, intuitive platform. Built with a premium "glassmorphism" aesthetic, it prioritizes a calming user experience while handling critical safety operations.

Core Modules & Features
1. Dynamic Physical Health Dashboard

Body Battery Metric: Calculates a real-time energy capacity score based on sleep logging, step counts, and stress levels.
Diagnostic Tools: Interactive symptom checking, diet recommendations, and medication tracking.
Organ System Health Check: Targeted inputs to assess the health of the Heart, Lungs, and Brain.
2. Mental Health & AI Companion

Intelligent Chatbot: A globally accessible, floating AI assistant trained to analyze emotional weight and offer empathetic, actionable advice.
Risk Detection: Natural Language Processing (NLP) designed to detect severe emotional distress or suicide risks and suggest immediate intervention.
Relax & Reset Hub: Built-in micro-games (Bubble Pop, Breathing Circles, Focus Tap) engineered for rapid stress relief and grounding.
3. Emergency SOS Hub (The Safety Net)

Rapid Activation: One-click SOS trigger that initiates intense screen flashing, a loud algorithmic siren, and mobile device vibration (SOS Morse code pattern).
Automated Dispatch: Immediately captures live GPS coordinates and dispatches them via SMS and Automated Voice Calls (via Twilio) to pre-defined "Safe Circle" contacts.
Hospital Routing: Integrates with map services to instantly locate and route the user to the nearest medical facilities.
Technology Stack
Frontend Framework: React.js (built with Vite for high performance)
Styling & UI: Tailwind CSS (for utility-class styling) and Framer Motion (for fluid, 60fps glassmorphism animations).
Backend Server: Node.js & Express.js
Database/Storage: LocalStorage (client-side data persistence)
External APIs & Integrations:
OpenAI / Groq API: Powers the conversational AI logic.
Twilio API: Handles emergency SMS and Voice call routing.
Nodemailer: Manages secondary emergency email dispatches.
Geolocation & Mapbox: Fetches live coordinates and reverse-geocodes addresses.
Web Audio & Vibration APIs: Triggers native hardware alarms.
Target Audience
Individuals seeking a centralized platform to manage chronic conditions, daily well-being, or mental health, as well as users who require a reliable digital safety net (e.g., the elderly, people working in high-risk environments, or individuals navigating personal safety concerns).

